flowchart TB
  accTitle: A collection references intelligence without widening access to it
  accDescr: A reader first needs access to the collection and its list of references. Each target is checked independently. A visible event can be opened; a private event remains restricted. An attribute value reference uses a SHA-256 address; the value text resolves only through an attribute visible to that reader. Sharing the collection does not grant access to its targets.
  R["Reader"] -->|"Collection access check"| C["Visible collection<br/>Metadata + references"]
  C -->|"Target access check"| E["Visible event<br/>Can be opened"]
  C -->|"Target access check"| P["Private event<br/>Remains restricted"]
  C -->|"Value reference"| V["SHA-256 address<br/>Text requires a visible attribute"]
  class R,C,E accent;
  class P,V caution;
